classes.definition:
THE ARROW. An attributed claim that a change in one Variable (the claimed cause, normally set by a Decision) produces a change in another Variable (the claimed effect), usually one in another function's remit. It records:
- sign;
- dependency kind (Pearl rung);
- orientation (forecast, explanation or standing);
- coarse magnitude band and lag window;
- mechanism and scope;
- the functions the claimant says originate and bear it;
- the carried kinds and handoff pathway alleged;
- cited evidence.
It is an n-ary node: no triple anywhere links the two Variables directly. Truth is the causal layer's verdict, written back only as an Appraisal. It subsumes every function's effect-claim class.

A body of evidence cited by the author of a claim or appraisal. It records:
- its design class (an EvidenceClass term, never ranked);
- its source system ('none: recollection' is a valid, visible value);
- its observation window;
- optionally a reproducible selection predicate and a comparison baseline (a ticket cohort is an EvidenceItem);
- the KG artefacts it rests on (cmp:Evidence, cmp:AuditFinding, lgl:Clause, fin:Transaction, log:Shipment).
It is neutral in itself. Whether it supports or undermines a claim depends on who cites it. It is deliberately not cmp:Evidence, which means 'a control operated' and carries a 90-day freshness rule.

extensionPoints.contract:
Select ?c a xfn:EffectClaim ; xfn:recordStatus 'asserted'.

Always present on every such claim:
- exactly one claimedCause and one claimedEffect: distinct xfn:Variable IRIs, and this pair is the key of the candidate edge;
- claimedSign, dependencyKind (the rung), orientation;
- at least one impactedFunction;
- attributedTo, onBehalfOf, recordedAt, and the claimant's verbatim statement.

Optional, and always the claimant's own quotation:
- magnitudeBand and magnitudeStatement;
- onsetLagMin and onsetLagMax (single-unit xsd:duration);
- temporalProfile, claimedMechanism, claimedMediator, effectModifier, scopeEntity;
- allegedPathway (Handoff IRIs);
- statedCredence and the likelihood term;
- conditionalOnModel.

When viaDecision is present:
- claimedCause is one of that decision's intervenesOn variables;
- baselineState to interventionState is the do() contrast;
- the decision's effectiveFrom is lag zero.

Immutability:
- content under an IRI never changes after draft, and contentDigest lets you verify that;
- a refinement is a new claim linked by revises;
- withdrawn and superseded claims remain queryable.

Guaranteed absences:
- no triple links two Variables;
- the claim set is not a DAG, is not complete, and may contain cycles;
- a pair of Variables that nobody has claimed about is unknown. Exclusions exist only as owned claims with claimedSign 'no-effect'.

Key: every observation references exactly one xfn:MetricVersion IRI, never a MetricDefinition. Use qb:Observation or dqv:isMeasurementOf, or a metric_version_iri column.

Admissibility:
- published versions, for observation dates on or after effectiveFrom;
- deprecated versions, for dates before the successor's effectiveFrom.

Coordinates:
- exactly one per DimensionBinding, ordered by dimensionOrder;
- each is a KG instance IRI of the dimension's memberClass, or the ISO date of a timeUnit period;
- the GrainDimension IRI itself means 'all members'.

Values:
- literals of valueDatatype, in unitIri/currencyCode;
- converted before binding, never at read time.

Layer 3's obligations:
- attest that the observed set satisfies populationClass + inclusionCriteria (+ populationPerspective);
- register its implementations keyed by version IRI.

xfn guarantees:
- a published version and its component closure (numerator, denominator, derivedFrom, bindings) never change;
- IRIs are never reused;
- xfn stores no value, now or later.

reconciledConflicts.modelledAs:
Kept as separate facts:
- stewardedBy, for definitions;
- Answerability, with accountabilityKind control-owner, cost-center, outcome-owner or definition-steward;
