There is no generic 'owner'.

anchorScenarioWalkthrough:
0. VOCABULARY.
xfn:BusinessFunction instances: procurement, finance, operations, support, legal and enterprise. They are performedBy the hr:OrgUnits that exist. Support and legal have none, and that absence is itself a finding.

xfn:Position seats: CPO, COO, VP-Support and GC, each solidLineTo CEO. CPO also has seatOn S&OP-Council.

xfn:DecisionDomain/SUPPLIER-SELECTION-DM has domainOwner procurement and actsOnClass fin:Vendor.

xfn:DecisionRight/DR-2025-0101: holder CPO, rightKind ratify, authorityLimit 5000000 USD, basis formal, grantedUnder cmp:Policy/POL-03. No consult or veto right is recorded for GC. That gap can be queried.

1. VARIABLES (xfn:Variable).
- V1 component-c-primary-supplier: categorical; aboutEntity log:InventoryItem/SKU-1042.
- V2 component-c-unit-price.
- V3 component-c-landed-cost: Finance's definition.
- V4 product-p-defect-ticket-rate: Support.
- V5 component-c-field-failure-rate.
- V6 eu-central-inbound-otif.
- V7 component-c-indemnity-cover: binary; Legal.
- V8 firmware-r7-deployed.

2. OUTCOMES (xfn:Outcome).
- O-unit-cost: statedOver V2, decrease, procurement.
- O-quality-contacts: statedOver V4, decrease, support.
- O-otif: statedOver V6, increase, operations.
- O-risk-transfer: statedOver V7, maintain, legal.
- O-tco: inRemitOf enterprise; hasConstituent all four above.

xfn:Answerability records: CPO answersFor O-unit-cost, VP-Support for O-quality-contacts, COO for O-otif, GC for O-risk-transfer. Each is answerableTo CEO.

3. METRICS.
xfn:MetricDefinition MET-001 'Procurement unit-cost saving': definedByFunction procurement, stewardedBy CPO.
Its MetricVersion 1.0 records:
- baselineDescription: 'last price paid, prior 4 quarters';
- recognitionEvent: 'PO issue at new price';
- grain: vendor + fiscal-period, recompute-from-components.

xfn:MetricBinding: CPO evaluated-on MET-001 for 2025-Q1..Q4.

Further definitions:
- MET-014 defect-ticket-rate (SKU + week);
- MET-021 OTIF (line grain, generation-1 boundary);
- MET-033 indemnity coverage.

xfn:ProxyClaim PR-0001, by the CPO on behalf of procurement: MET-001 is a proxy for O-tco.
- coversOutcome: only O-unit-cost;
- validityCondition: 'like-for-like spec, quality tier, delivery terms and risk allocation incl. indemnity'.

4. DECISION.
xfn:Decision/PROC-2025-014:
- decisionKind supplier-switch; inDecisionDomain SUPPLIER-SELECTION-DM; exercisedRight DR-2025-0101;
- decidedBy the CPO person, decidedInCapacityOf CPO, decidingFunction procurement;
- decidedOn 2024-12-02, effectiveFrom 2025-01-15, status enacted;
- intervenesOn V1;
- baselineState 'V-2305 under ACME-CTR-0017'; interventionState 'V-2688 under ACME-CTR-0101';
- changesObject supply-component-c;
- involvesEntity both fin:Vendors and both lgl:Contracts;
- consultedFunction {finance}, consultationComplete true;
- statedBenefitMetric MET-001; declaredScope local; reversalLeadTimeDays 270.

xfn:Commitment for a 3-year minimum volume:
- isContractual false, capturedIn price-file, exitTerms '12 months notice'.
Its xfn:Transfer (carriesKind obligation, transferTo operations) is unacknowledged.

5. IDENTITY.
The instance BoundaryObject supply-component-c exemplifies the ideal type 'supply arrangement'. Its Perspectives are revisedBy PROC-2025-014:
- procurement and finance: representedBy fin:Vendor/V-2688;
- legal v2: representedBy lgl:Contract/ACME-CTR-0101. It revises legal v1, which pointed at ACME-CTR-0017;
- operations: representedBy log:PurchaseOrder/...;
- support: criterion only, no record.

The BoundaryObject for NewCo has aboutEntity xfn:LegalEntity/P-000412 (LEI, parentEntity). Nobody stewards it.

6. THE SAVING.
xfn:EffectClaim EC-2025-0101:
- CPO on behalf of procurement, recordedAt 2024-11-20;
- V1 -> V2 viaDecision PROC-2025-014;
- claimedSign decrease; magnitudeStatement '-12% unit price'; magnitudeBand material;
- dependencyKind interventional; orientation prospective; onsetLagMin P0D;
- citesEvidence EV-01 (documentary-record: the quotes);
- impactedFunction procurement.
It is a claim like any other. Being on a scorecard gives it no special truth.

7. THE MISSING INDEMNITY.
xfn:TermDeviation TD-2025-007, recorded by GC:
- deviationInContract ACME-CTR-0101; termKind indemnity; direction absent;
- benchmarkContract ACME-CTR-0017, benchmarkClause its Indemnification clause;
- deviationApprovedBy empty.

EC-2025-0144, by GC on behalf of legal:
- V1 -> V7, decrease, counterfactual, lag P0D, virtually-certain;
- evidence EV-05 (documentary-record over both contracts);
- impactedFunction legal and enterprise.

On the procurement->legal contract-handover Handoff, a Transfer records:
- carriesKind risk, passesAt 'contract execution', acceptanceStatus unacknowledged, basis contractual;
- refersToItem a cmp:Risk.

8. THE OTIF SLIP.
EC-2025-0143, by the COO on behalf of operations:
- V1 -> V6, decrease, magnitudeStatement '-4pp', counterfactual, lag P3M-P6M;
- allegedPathway: the procurement->operations onboarding Handoff; allegedKind risk;
- evidence EV-04: observational, evidenceSource log:Shipment/SHP-001..010;
- impactedFunction operations.

9. THE TICKET RISE (the arrow).
EC-2025-0142, by VP-Support on behalf of support, recordedAt 2025-08-04:
- V1 -> V4 viaDecision PROC-2025-014; claimedMediator V5;
- increase; band material; '+15-45%';
- counterfactual, retrospective, lag P5M-P7M, accumulating;
- mechanism: 'new supplier not qualified at part-revision grain';
- evidence EV-02: observational-analysis, source Zendesk, selectionCriteria defines the ticket cohort, comparisonBaseline EV-02b covers the prior two quarters;
- evidence EV-03: case-anecdote, 23 RMA teardowns;
- originFunction procurement; impactedFunction support; status asserted.

The saving (EC-0101) and the tickets (EC-0142) are both effects of the same decision, joined at PROC-2025-014. Nothing asserts saving -> tickets, and nothing asserts either claim is true.

10. CONTEST.
xfn:Appraisal AP-2025-0031, by the CPO on behalf of procurement, disputes EC-0142:
- onAspect alternative-cause and magnitude;
- invokesVariable V8;
- advances EC-2025-0151: V8 -> V4 via Decision ENG-2025-R7.

Finance's AP-0032 disputes EC-0101 on variable-definition and advances EC-0160: V1 -> V3, '-3% [-6,+1]'.

xfn:DivergenceClaim KD-0001, by VP-Support, is divergenceOf PR-0001:
- modes externality, horizon-mismatch, multitask-omission;
- outcomeAtRisk O-quality-contacts, O-otif, O-risk-transfer;
- observableVia MET-014/021/033;
- mechanismClaim EC-0142/0143/0144.

11. REVIEW AND LAYER 2.
xfn:Deliberation DL-2025-019 (decision-review) is convenedBy the CEO and concernsDecision PROC-2025-014.
- The claims were generatedIn it: Support, Operations and Legal were solicited; Procurement volunteered.
- Layer 2 later writes Appraisal AP-0077, by xfn:AnalyticAgent/causal-engine-0.9 with conditionalOnModel supply-quality-dag/v7. It qualifies EC-0142 on magnitude and advances the engine's own EC-0170.

12. DERIVED, WITH NO VALUES STORED.
Rule exposure-gap@1.0 emits three xfn:ExposureGap nodes. Each pairs DR-2025-0101 with one bearer: VP-Support via EC-0142, COO via EC-0143, GC via EC-0144. All three converge at CEO with no shared forum.

Queries now expose:
- a variety deficit: support, operations and legal were affected but not consulted;
- no Support -> Procurement return Handoff;
- 3 of the 4 O-tco constituents unproxied;
- a clause regression: TD-2025-007;
- an unaccepted risk Transfer.
